# Patch for rules_python to support local wheel overrides (local_wheels in pip.parse).
#
# Changes:
# 1. python/private/pypi/extension.bzl:
#    - Adds the `local_wheels` attribute (string_dict) to the `pip.parse` extension tag class.
#    - Passes `is_root = mod.is_root` to restrict local wheel overrides to the root module.
#
# 2. python/private/pypi/hub_builder.bzl:
#    - Adds `_collect_local_wheels` to discover matching .whl files from workspace-relative paths or globs (e.g. dist/scipy-*.whl).
#    - In `_create_whl_repos`, when PyPI has no matching wheels for the target Python version (leaving whl.srcs empty),
#      synthesizes target platform source entries pointing to the local wheel override so Bazel select() aliases resolve correctly.
#    - In `_whl_repo`, handles `local_wheel` upfront to construct a file:/// wheel repo before checking download_only or sdist fallbacks.
#
# 3. python/private/pypi/urllib.bzl:
#    - In `_strip_empty_path_segments`, preserves the scheme if scheme == "file" so that "file:///path/to/wheel.whl"
#      is not collapsed to "file://path/to/wheel.whl" (which causes Java's URL downloader to fail with UnknownHostException).

